# jwks-server environment variables
# Copy to .env for local development — DO NOT commit real key material.
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PREFERRED: ADMIN_JWKS_B64  (base64-encoded JWKS JSON)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Why use base64?
#   Passing raw JSON via Railway CLI / PowerShell often breaks due to
#   quote escaping. Base64 is a plain alphanumeric string — zero quoting issues.
#
# How to generate (run locally, NEVER commit jwks.json or the private key):
#
#   Step 1 — Generate keypair (outside repo):
#     openssl genrsa -out ~/admin-private.pem 2048
#     openssl rsa -in ~/admin-private.pem -pubout -out ~/admin-public.pem
#
#   Step 2 — Convert public key to JWKS JSON (node make-jwks.js from jwks/ dir)
#     node make-jwks.js   # produces jwks.json
#
#   Step 3 — Base64-encode the JWKS JSON (PowerShell):
#     [Convert]::ToBase64String([Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes((Get-Content -Raw jwks.json)))
#
#   Step 3 — Base64-encode the JWKS JSON (bash/zsh):
#     base64 -w0 jwks.json
#
#   Step 4 — Set in Railway (no quoting issues):
#     railway variables set "ADMIN_JWKS_B64=<the-base64-string>" --service jwks-server
#
# ADMIN_JWKS_B64=<base64url-encoded-jwks-json>

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# FALLBACK: ADMIN_JWKS_PAYLOAD  (raw JSON string — legacy)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Only use if ADMIN_JWKS_B64 is not available.
# JSON quoting in PowerShell can corrupt this value — prefer ADMIN_JWKS_B64.
#
# Contains ONLY public fields (kty, n, e, use, kid, alg).
# NEVER include private fields (d, p, q, dp, dq, qi) — server will reject them.
#
# Template (replace n with real base64url modulus):
# ADMIN_JWKS_PAYLOAD={"keys":[{"kty":"RSA","n":"<base64url-modulus>","e":"AQAB","use":"sig","kid":"admin-key-2","alg":"RS256"}]}

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PORT
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Default: 3001. Railway overrides this automatically.
PORT=3001
